## Working on the Project

- pi reads this file (`AGENTS.md`) as project context; it also supports `CLAUDE.md`, and per-project `.pi/APPEND_SYSTEM.md` (appends to the system prompt) / `.pi/SYSTEM.md` (replaces it)
- Role commands from the pi-development-kit (when installed): `/build-tdd`, `/build-debug`, `/build-quick-work`, `/build-docs`, `/plan-bdd` work as main-session roles; `/diff-review`, `/solid-review`, `/world-review` delegate to isolated subagents
- Consult `.pi/skills/` for project-specific patterns and gotchas
- Capture learnings in `[docs directory]/learnings/` after significant discoveries
- Use the `capturing-learnings` skill for structured post-session debriefs
